Allow large variable-label runs from gLabels' own print view.

The upstream UI limits the page-count spin box to 250.  That forces users to
fall back to the Windows copy count, but copies made by the system print dialog
repeat an already-rendered page and therefore do not advance gLabels variables.

Keep the finite QSpinBox safeguard, but raise it to a practical 999999 pages.
This only changes input validation; it does not pre-allocate pages or printer
memory.  Large runs should still be submitted in manageable batches.

diff --git a/glabels/ui/PrintView.ui b/glabels/ui/PrintView.ui
--- a/glabels/ui/PrintView.ui
+++ b/glabels/ui/PrintView.ui
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@
              <number>1</number>
             </property>
             <property name="maximum">
-             <number>250</number>
+             <number>999999</number>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
